<title>GERMANY: Prodi says did not ask for exceptions for EMU.</title>
<headline>Prodi says did not ask for exceptions for EMU.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian prime minister Romano Prodi said on Friday he did not ask for any special treatment in assessing Italy's efforts to join Europe's planned currency union at a meeting with Germany's Chancellor Helmut Kohl.</p>
<p>In a speech delivered after the meeting with Kohl, Prodi said &quot;I have asked for no exceptions to be made. I have not asked for support. Why should I?&quot;</p>
<p>He also said Europe would not be complete without Italy's participation. &quot;There can be no complete Europe without Italy.&quot;</p>
</text>
